meta {
  name: Send program link email
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/send-links/initiatives?program=ASH&type=REGISTRATION
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "user@example.com",
    "name": "John Doe"
  }
}

params:query {
  program: ASH
  type: REGISTRATION
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:3000
}

docs {
  # Send Program Link Email
  
  Sends a program-specific link (registration or feedback form) to a recipient via email. The service renders an EJS email template based on the `program` and `type` query parameters, then dispatches the email using Brevo.
  
  ## Endpoint
  `POST /api/v1/send-links/initiatives`
  
  ## Query Parameters
  
  | Parameter | Type | Required | Allowed Values | Description |
  | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
  | `program` | string | Yes | `ASH`, `TACOTS`, `VOLUNTEER` | The program whose link should be sent. |
  | `type` | string | Yes | `REGISTRATION`, `FEEDBACK` | The type of form link to send. |
  
  ## Request Body
  The request expects a JSON object with the following fields:
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Constraints | Description |
  | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
  | `email` | string | Yes | Must be a valid email address | The recipient's email address. |
  | `name` | string | Yes | Min: 3 characters, Max: 256 characters | The recipient's name (used in the email template). |
  
  ## Link Mapping
  The generated form link is derived from `FRONTEND_BASEURL` and the `program`/`type` combination:
  
  | Program | Type | Generated Link Path |
  | :--- | :--- | :--- |
  | `ASH` | `REGISTRATION` | `/social-initiatives/ash/register` |
  | `ASH` | `FEEDBACK` | `/social-initiatives/ash/feedback` |
  | `TACOTS` | `REGISTRATION` | `/social-initiatives/tacots/recommendation` |
  | `TACOTS` | `FEEDBACK` | `/social-initiatives/tacots/feedback` |
  | `VOLUNTEER` | `REGISTRATION` | `/get-involved/volunteer/register` |
  | `VOLUNTEER` | `FEEDBACK` | `/get-involved/volunteer/feedback` |
  
  ## Success Response
  - **Status Code**: `200 OK`
  - **Body**:
    ```json
    {
      "success": true,
      "message": "ASH REGISTRATION email sent successfully"
    }
    ```
  
  > The `message` field dynamically reflects the `program` and `type` values used in the request.
  
  ## Error Responses
  - **400 Bad Request**: Validation failed (e.g., invalid email, name too short, invalid `program` or `type` enum value).
  - **429 Too Many Requests**: Rate limit exceeded (`sendLinksLimiter`: 5 requests per 15-minute window, keyed by IP).
  - **500 Internal Server Error**: 
    - Failed to render the EJS email template.
    - Brevo API error (email transporter failure).
    - Email delivery verification failed — thrown when `sendEmail` returns a falsy value (e.g., `"ASH Registration Email was not sent"`).
  
  ## Rate Limiting
  This endpoint is protected by `sendLinksLimiter` — a maximum of **5 requests per 15-minute window**, keyed by the client's IP address. Exceeds return a `429` with `{ code: "RATE_LIMITED", message: "Too many request attempts. Please try again later" }`.
  
  ## Notes
  - Each `program`/`type` combination uses a dedicated EJS template (e.g., `ash-registration-link.ejs`, `tacots-feedback-link.ejs`).
  - No caching is involved — this endpoint triggers a transactional email on every call.
}
